# Build-context exclusions.
#
# Two kinds of target build from the repository root: the local-cloud image
# (deploy/local-cloud/docker-compose.yml uses `context: ../..`) and
# docker/ios-grindercore/Dockerfile, which compose runs with `context: ..`.  The
# Python, PHP, Node and firmware-triage targets use docker/ as their context and
# are unaffected by this file.
#
# Without it every one of those builds ships the whole research tree to the
# daemon: the vendor firmware releases under firmware/ are the bulk of it, and
# none of them is ever COPYed.  A smaller context is a faster build, and it keeps
# unrelated files out of the layer-cache key, where they would invalidate a build
# that changed nothing the image reads.
#
# Keep this list about *context size and provenance*.  It must not name a path
# an image actually COPYs, so the entries are deliberately coarse and the
# service package (tools/local_cloud) is not excluded.

# Vendor firmware, captures and locally extracted toolchains: fetched or
# produced, never baked in.
firmware/
*.swu
captures/
.tools/
decaid/

# Repository metadata and history.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# Build output from the app trees.  Both depths are needed, because Docker's `*`
# does not cross `/`: `apps/*/build/` matches apps/android/build, and only
# `apps/*/*/build/` matches apps/android/app/build, which is the exact path
# docs/REPRODUCIBLE_BUILDS.md §1 names as the Android artifact.  The same holds
# for the SwiftPM tree under apps/ios/GrinderCore/.build.
apps/*/build/
apps/*/*/build/
apps/*/.build/
apps/*/*/.build/
dist/

# Local credentials.  .gitignore already ignores these, and the root-context
# builds would otherwise carry a real token: the documented
# `cp deploy/local-cloud/.env.example deploy/local-cloud/.env` produces exactly
# this file.  `**/` compiles to `(.*/)?`, so the two patterns below cover the
# context root as well as every subdirectory, and bare `.env` lines would be
# redundant rather than load-bearing.  `**/.env.*` also drops the shipped
# `.env.example`, which no image reads.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Interpreter leftovers: the service image copies *.py only, and these would
# only add noise to the context.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store
